# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Oaxaca-Puebla-Rail .gitignore
#
# Policy: raw source documents are NOT committed. Their URL, publisher and
# retrieval date are recorded in deliverables/data_sources.md so any source can
# be re-fetched. Extracted markdown/JSON IS committed - it is the traceable
# evidence chain that deliverables cite.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Raw sources (reproducible from data_sources.md, not committed) --------
sources/raw/**
!sources/raw/.gitkeep

# --- Model weights / ML caches ---------------------------------------------
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.onnx
*.gguf
.cache/huggingface/
huggingface/
hf_cache/
.huggingface/
transformers_cache/
torch_hub/
models/weights/
*.mlpackage/

# --- Virtualenvs / Python --------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.conda/
conda-env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.Python
pip-wheel-metadata/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Large binaries (hard rule: nothing over 50MB is committed) ------------
# Enforced by analysis/scripts/check_repo_hygiene.sh, which fails on any
# staged blob >50MB. Common offenders listed explicitly:
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
*.gpkg
*.mbtiles
*.laz
*.las
*.tif
*.tiff
*.img
*.sqlite
*.duckdb

# --- OS / editor noise -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# --- Office lock files (breakeven_model.xlsx itself IS committed) ----------
~$*.xlsx
~$*.docx
.~lock.*
